    <statement><p>A point mass of 2 grams located 3 centimeters to the left of the
origin and a point mass of 4 grams located 6 centimeters to the 
right of the origin are connected by a thin, light rod.  Find
the center of mass of the system.</p>
<p>Center of Mass = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
<ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0002"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>to the left of the origin</p>
</li><li>
<p>to the right of the origin</p>
</li><li>
<p>(at the origin)</p>
</li></ul></p>
<p>(include 
in your center of mass)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\ {\rm cm}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{to the right of the origin}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\overline{x} =\frac{2(-3)+4(6)}{6} =
  3\ {\rm cm} \hbox{ to right of origin.}</me>



</solution>
